    "result": "All tests pass! Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n**Issue 1: Missing named exports in governance module**\n- The test file imported `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named import from the governance index, but it was only available through the default export\n- **Fix**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` while keeping the default export intact for backward compatibility\n\n**Issue 2: Toxicity metric function signature mismatch**\n- The `toxicityMetric` function signature was `(outputs, bannedTerms)`, but `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)` \n- This caused the references array to be interpreted as banned terms, incorrectly flagging all outputs\n- **Fix**: Updated the signature to `(outputs, references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` to match the calling convention, with a safety check to ensure `bannedTerms` is actually an array before using it\n\nBoth changes maintain full backward compatibility with existing code. All 28 tests now pass.",
